WEBVTT

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:13.950
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:14.150
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.110
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:43.120
<b>Chapter Five                      Silver Hope</b>

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.600
I wasn't able to show you

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.960
even half of what you wanted to see, was I?

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:46.870
It's all right.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.760
I can go again whenever I want.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.880
It must be fun to be able to fly a plane.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.350
You could go somewhere no one else is.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.760
Do you want to go somewhere you'd be alone?

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.310
I do.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:00.260
Deep in the mountains or an isolated island...

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.110
Be self-sufficient, make yourself 
a home with only a knife.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.700
Fishing, gathering plants...

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.050
The ultimate freedom.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.950
Why don't you do it?

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.400
Because there are things that hold me back.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.780
I can't abandon everything.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.590
You, yourself, are right here.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.650
So you won't lose everything.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.140
But in other words...

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.360
Perhaps I'm scared.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.470
I'm just a normal man—

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.150
That doesn't matter!

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.510
I'm sorry.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.920
No, it was my fault.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.800
Did you cry?

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.930
When it happened, I'm certain there 
was someone next to you.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.700
There wasn't anyone...

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.190
Then I shall change my question.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.100
You lost your parents, did you not?

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.610
Do you remember that day?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.820
What were you wearing?

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.550
Purple...

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.230
Nishinosono-kun, can I come in?

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.160
Yes.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.710
Want some coffee?

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.050
Is it a little too hot for you?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.220
Why is coffee always too hot?

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.750
It isn't always too hot.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.630
That's just how it seems to you.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:27.890
I know that!

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.320
Did you have a bad dream?

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.160
Mornings like this feel like a shampoo hat.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.300
I don't think that's true.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.430
Is my voice weird?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.470
No? It's husky and quite attractive.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.140
You're being nice today, aren't you?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.260
Do you know the difference 
between kindness and love?

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.310
Each word has a different number of letters.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.690
What was your dream like?

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.710
It was a dream about that night.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.220
That night?

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.850
The night my parents died.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:09.150
Dr. Magata asked me,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.230
"Do you remember that day?"

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.180
"Did you cry?"

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.770
"When it happened, I'm certain there 
was someone next to you."

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.190
But I was alone.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:25.000
I was always alone...

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.930
That's enough. Thanks for telling me.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.460
Sensei, why do people live?

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.700
I've answered that question many times.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.210
You shouldn't be

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.270
someone who can't stand on 
their own at times like this.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.750
You should rest a little longer.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.020
What am I doing?

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.400
I'm the one who's confused.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.280
Saikawa-sensei?

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.320
Good morning.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.150
This is the director's wife.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.930
I'm Shindo Yumiko.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.780
Hello.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.960
Um, would you like to try these?

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.120
I made too many.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.740
Cookies?

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.910
Yes. Do you not like sweets?

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.220
No, I do.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.130
Nishinosono-kun, there are cookies out here!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.130
You like them, right?

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.630
How are you feeling?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.140
Oh, I'm fine now!

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.400
I don't know what to say about 
what happened yesterday.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.700
Don't worry about it.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:39.370
Talking to everyone like this keeps my mind off it.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.330
I see.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:47.330
What do you suppose Miki-san will do now?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.660
It seems she's planning to return to America.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.400
Oh, that's right.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.050
Supposedly, Miki-san's bag is still in the helicopter.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.800
Yamane-san, could you take a look later?

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.490
It has a present for Shiki-san.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.310
All right. I'll look later.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.180
Um... Could you tell me about Dr. Magata?

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.180
About Shiki-san?

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:10.980
Yes.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.730
Well, hmm...

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.430
She was a lovely young lady.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:18.780
Though she'd get upset if you told her that.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.810
Of course, she was extremely bright.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.710
But to me, she was just my cute little niece.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.320
Why did she kill her parents?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.740
Nishinosono-kun.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.820
Sensei, please...

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.710
I don't know why.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.710
Fifteen years ago, your husband was at 
the scene of the murders, wasn't he?

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:38.910
That's enough.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.010
It's fine.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.920
Yes. He was.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.320
When she went inside,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.200
Shiki-san's father, Sachiro-san...

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.780
His wife was already lying on the floor.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:58.260
Shiki-san was covered in blood and holding a knife.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.480
He was grabbing her hand from behind...

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.480
Yes, that's right. I remember now.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.650
You remember what?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.000
He screamed.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Who did?

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.440
Sachiro-san.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:13.490
As he fell to the ground, he screamed, 
"I won't let you do this!"

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.870
What did he mean?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.090
Let her do what?

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:17.740
That's enough, Nishinosono-kun.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.250
It isn't.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.840
And then what happened to Dr. Magata?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.340
When she heard those words,

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.310
she screamed like she was possessed...

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.360
And then,

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.760
she started to laugh.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.120
Kurimoto Kishio.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.770
Sasaki Suma.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.780
Oh, you know about them?

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.490
The other is Magata Michiru, yes?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.400
Yes, they're all Dr. Magata's...

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.280
Yes.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.290
She would always pretend to be those three.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.470
At first, it was only Kurimoto Kishio-san.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.460
Who was Kishio-san?

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.970
Her brother.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.140
She had a brother?

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:09.300
Yes.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.840
Oh, please try these.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.930
Thank you.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.880
The two were twins, supposedly.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:22.310
But I heard that he died right after their birth.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.180
Then, the other two?

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:29.320
Evidently, Sasaki Suma was 
based on Morikawa Suma,

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:33.400
her maid when she was in America.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.790
Where is this Suma-san now?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.070
She died in an accident.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:40.580
The shock was sufficient

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.460
to make Shiki-san stop working 
in America and return here.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.590
And then she started to imitate them?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.190
It went far beyond the level of "imitation."

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.540
She created their internal personalities.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.360
It was like they were real people.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.010
The inside of Shiki-san's head

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.260
may have been too big for just one personality.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.530
And who is Magata Michiru-san?

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:06.690
A doll.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:07.920
A doll?

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.200
The name of the doll she brought here,

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.150
when she came to this lab.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.070
Where is it now?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.640
It was covered in blood, so we threw it out.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.970
I'm sorry for asking all this...

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.750
No, it's fine.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.290
Thank you.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.710
Nishinosono-kun?

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.260
They're really good.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.720
I ate too much.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.460
They were really good.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.700
But why did she make so many cookies?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.030
I'm sure there's no reason.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.210
She just wanted to do something.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.530
I understand.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.750
What will you do for breakfast?

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.470
Oh, I'm fine.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.970
I had those cookies.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:17.970
I'd like something.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.670
You're still going to eat?

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:20.970
Leave me alone.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.470
It's nice to be young.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.470
<b>Shimada Ayako 

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.420
That's the first good news I've had in a while.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.850
"This is Shimada.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.880
<b>Shimada Ayako</b>

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:36.350
I'd totally forgotten, but Dr. Magata had a meeting

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:39.550
with a writer from a women's magazine tomorrow.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.830
The writer is coming to the lab.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.880
In other words, a ship will be coming tomorrow."

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.590
That's great news, huh?

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.140
I'm so relieved.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:49.620
Only a little, though.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.830
Will toast be okay?

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.060
You like bread, right?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.510
<b>Bread</b>

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.240
Huh?

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:04.110
Um, what do you have to do

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:07.020
to open that aluminum door on Dr. Magata's side?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.410
That's under Deborah's control.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.020
Only authorized personnel can 
open it from this side.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.760
It can also be opened from her side,

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.710
but only she has the ability to do so.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.530
Like the other doors, you put your hand up to it...

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.580
I had the same initial idea.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.160
They needed her right hand to open that door?

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.070
The killer used her severed right 
hand to open the door?

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.190
The killer still has her hand and is 
wandering around the building?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.020
I can't say it's impossible,

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.360
but I don't think that's the case anymore.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.680
Come to think of it,

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.740
we need to take her body back to her room.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.530
Have you figured out the case yet, Sensei?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.600
No, I haven't been trying.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.870
You're never honest with me.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.800
But there is something I've been wondering about.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.190
What is it?

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:25.620
How did the killer get in,

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.040
and how did they get out?

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.350
Getting through the lab's security 
system is impossible.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.360
Then what if they were in that room before 
the security cameras were installed?

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.190
For fifteen years?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.380
Those logical leaps are characteristic 
of the way you think.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.750
But right now, I'm more interested in 
what happened fifteen years ago.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:50.870
So it seems.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.060
A doll did it.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.950
Was she talking about Michiru?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.170
I don't know.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.860
But I have no idea what it means 
for a doll to kill a person.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.890
A "doll" may mean a human body.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.890
She meant a human body?

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:12.390
Yes. A body, as a vessel for a soul.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.180
She told you that she alone was seven, right?

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:21.900
Yes, and that seven was the only lonely number.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.080
That's it.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:25.590
What does that mean?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.120
There were multiple personalities within her.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.670
But she was alone, and the others weren't.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.030
Why?

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.880
Because she was the only one with a body.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.750
Then she, herself, was the doll?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.680
All the other personalities were dead people.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.920
Why was that the case?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:45.850
I don't know.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:48.760
Perhaps she was overtaken by death.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.540
But Michiru is the only one that wasn't dead.

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.810
Was there a Michiru who wasn't a doll?

00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:02.690
And the words that Dr. Magata's 
father said before he fell...

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.190
"I won't let you do this."

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:09.340
Was he talking about being stabbed with a knife?

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:14.340
Or had he been arguing with Dr. Magata?

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.170
But would that have been enough to kill him over?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.830
It isn't impossible, depending on the situation.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.290
What situation could there be?

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.660
For example, this is only a hypothesis,

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.340
but Magata Shiki may have been

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:31.070
unable to forgive anyone who would 
trespass on her own freedoms.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.860
Freedoms?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.000
Yes.

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:37.630
A person capable of anything

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.130
must experience great pain

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.310
when they're told not to do something.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.990
"I won't let you do this,"

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:48.910
is what someone who thinks they're 
in a position of authority says.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.880
Well, he was her father.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.250
But he was talking to Magata Shiki.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:55.310
I can't imagine

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.550
she would let anyone interfere with 
her actions, even her parents.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.060
Even if that's true,

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.780
there must've been a way to obtain 
freedom without killing anyone.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.500
Such as?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.460
Escaping.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.050
Running away from home.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.260
I see.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.530
I think about that a lot, too.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:15.240
I want to be released from 
those god-awful meetings,

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.530
and become free.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:18.770
Sometimes, I want to just quit the university.

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:21.650
You've been thinking that, Sensei?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.340
It's only an example.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.550
I haven't actually made the choice to quit.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.280
Why?

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.170
To put it simply, I'm tied down.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.150
If you want to quit, then quit!

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.520
Yes...

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.110
You're right.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:40.980
You should just quit and work on 
whatever research you like.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.350
There's no need for someone with your talent

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.380
to waste time on faculty meetings.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.390
If it were me...

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:47.300
If it were you?

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.440
I could give you that environment.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:52.000
Nishinosono-kun, that wouldn't be right.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.480
What wouldn't?

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.030
That would only be another chain.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.430
A chain?

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.930
You think I'd tie you down?

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.270
No, the opposite.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.480
It would tie you down.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.600
I don't care if you tie me down.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.410
Even if you don't care, I do.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.030
Why would you say something so sad?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.990
It's the same with Dr. Magata.

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:18.760
I think it's love that causes parents to 
restrict their children's freedom.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.430
Some disagree.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:24.650
Then, to escape those constraints,

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.850
you think it's okay to kill people?

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:28.410
That's quite a leap.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.920
Don't try and change the subject!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:33.840
Nishinosono-kun,

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.350
my opinion isn't what's important here.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.630
The important question is what 
Dr. Magata was thinking.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:42.630
Does it matter? She killed her parents.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:44.890
No matter how much she valued her freedom,

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:48.860
that means there was something 
lacking in her as a person!

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:51.400
No, we're the ones lacking something.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.440
Because there's something lacking in us,

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.850
we think about things like "human nature."

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.520
We make rules like "love" and "ethics."

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.340
We follow them, to compensate for 
something within us that's lacking.

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:09.670
So you're saying that love and ethics 
are just worthless rules?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.950
I'm not saying that.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:15.860
I'm saying that our morals and hers are different.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.430
And she's the one who's right.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.580
I don't know if she's right or not, but...

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.810
No one is as pure as Magata Shiki.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:26.270
Pure?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:30.250
To me, she seems selfish and overcomplicated!

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:32.820
"Selfish and overcomplicated" 
is humanity's natural state.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.380
I don't think any of us, as children, 
had only a single personality.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.000
We constantly contradicted ourselves,

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.080
and thought in a more diverse way than we do now.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.560
But as we grow,

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:47.760
we try to unify into one personality
 without contradictions,

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.360
to go along with our one body.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:54.340
And so, in the end, everyone is 
tied down by their bodies.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.450
Don't you find that terribly restrictive?

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:00.840
I've never felt restricted.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.650
I do, constantly.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.600
But unlike everyone else,

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.320
Dr. Magata didn't unify her personalities.

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:11.220
She maintained several independent personalities.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:15.080
I think that is a purer state of humanity.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:18.110
You could say that people like Dr. Magata

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.650
are the most human of us all.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.870
That's what you like about her. Isn't it, Sensei?

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:29.520
I'm not talking about whether I like her or not.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:31.880
I'm glad she's gone.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.880
Nishinosono-kun, I think that's rude to the doctor.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.140
You don't know anything, Sensei.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.620
I wouldn't kill my parents, no matter what happened!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.560
You and Dr. Magata are different people.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:01.180
There's no need to think the same things.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:06.720
No one can feel things the same 
way as another does, anyway.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.610
No matter how close they may be.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:13.430
So...

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.060
So what?

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.920
From now on, you should decide 
what you're going to do yourself.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.340
I'm going back to the camp.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.310
Do what you want. I don't care what you do!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.670
I won't say that.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:32.650
If all this didn't matter,

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.360
I wouldn't have come here.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:40.080
Even if I did have the chance to meet Dr. Magata.

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:46.850
A knife?

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:47.330
Yes.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.710
What will you use it for? Making something?

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.550
No.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.840
I want to go look for herbs at the 
campground or cut open fish.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.880
Oh, then...

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.430
Maybe this?

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.150
I'll take it.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.980
<b>Magata Labs Complete!</b>

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.980
I can't believe you have a building without windows.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:21.760
Can you really live here?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.380
Shall I at least put up some curtains?

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.930
At least you could tell yourself there are windows.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:27.820
Well...

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.400
Congratulations on your move.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.630
Oh, you're early.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:43.350
Congratulations, Shiki.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.010
Thank you, Uncle.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.210
It's going to be a fun party today.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.160
Help me, dear.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.270
Right, right.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.730
Happy birthday, Uncle.

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:56.970
Thank you.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:00.230
I have a present for you.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:01.890
What could it be?

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.440
A tool to free oneself.

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.040
<i>Free...</i>

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.800
<i>I realized what she meant,</i>

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.920
<i>and I felt my body shake</i>

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:24.060
<i>with terror and joy.</i>
